// Design stats (Round 36.11, Eddie 2026-11-20: "make the HP stats
// for the other characters — make sure it's a fun battle").
//
// The designed collection (utils/collectionDesigns.ts) shipped as
// CARD DATA ONLY: no battle stats. In battle, owner-mode records
// for the designs were derived from a flat per-tier ladder (every
// Mortal identical, every Ascendant identical), and their cards
// printed name + element with no stat block at all. This module is
// the designs' own stat table — one authored block per design,
// keyed by name, in the FightClub record's own shape
// (level / strength / defense / speed / stamina).
//
// THE BAND (derived from the fighters who already had stats —
// the hand-tuned DEMO_OPPONENTS in NavitarFightClub.tsx, whose
// card stats in sampleNavitars.ts are the same numbers in card
// shape): level 4–30, strength 45–95, defense 50–88, speed
// 55–95, stamina 4–10 (HP pool 130–250 at 50 + stamina × 20).
// Every entry below sits INSIDE that band — nothing outclasses
// the strongest existing fighter. Within the band, each design's
// build follows its visible character (hulking designs tankier,
// slight ones faster) and its tier (Primes at the band's top end).
//
// PRIME ZERO is the one deliberate exception in shape only: his
// entry repeats EXACTLY the numbers his owner record already
// derived from the tier ladder (Lv 30, 95/88/90, stamina 14), so
// his battle record is bit-identical before and after this round.
// His HP pool (330) stays his alone.
//
// Fighters who already had canonical stats are NOT here — the 9
// showcase heroes, the venue fighters (Frostpup, Ashwing,
// Tidecaller, Stonehorn, Coralight, Starborn, Voltkit, Wavefang,
// Leafpaw), the wild pair (Duskmoth, Quibble) and Griffin keep
// their own records, untouched.

